# Settings for the bundled price service. Copy this file to config\mandi-service.env
# (that copy is git-ignored, so keys are never committed). tools\start-mandi-service.ps1
# reads it. One KEY=VALUE per line; delete the lines you do not need.

# Needed for the Ask Mandi Setu advisory page (Gemini). Free key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# Without it the advisory still answers, with a plain template reply from the price data.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Optional own data.gov.in key for the daily fetch (not needed by the service itself).
# DATA_GOV_API_KEY=

# Optional shared secret protecting /advisory, /compare-advisory and /voice-advisory.
# If you set it here, set the SAME value as 'api_secret' in config\mandi.local.php.
# Left empty, the advisory endpoints answer only callers on this same machine (the normal AnnaSetu
# setup: PHP calls 127.0.0.1) and refuse everyone else with 503. Set it only if AnnaSetu and the
# price service run on different machines.
# If a web server (nginx/Apache) on this machine sits in front of the service, make it send an
# X-Forwarded-For header; a request carrying it is never treated as local (even if it claims
# 127.0.0.1), but without it every caller looks local and the check lets them in.
# API_SHARED_SECRET=
